-- Tankbook backend, migration 019 (CIS vehicle catalog seed: Chinese and Russian
-- makes sold in Russia and Kazakhstan).
--
-- docs/SCHEMA.md "Vehicle catalog", docs/SYNC.md "Reference data". The server is
-- the master copy of the catalog, and until now the published table started
-- empty: every device fell back to the bundled seed pack, which is built around
-- European and Japanese lines and misses the makes that dominate the CIS market.
-- A driver typing "Haval Jolion" or "Moskvich 3" got no pre-fill at all, so tank
-- capacity - which feeds partial-fill math and the OCR volume sanity check - had
-- to be typed by hand or left wrong.
--
-- This migration publishes 293 entries as one pack, in two halves.
--
-- 1. What is sold NEW: the Chinese brands on sale in Russia and Kazakhstan
--    (Haval, Chery, Geely, Changan, Exeed, Omoda, Jaecoo, Jetour, Tank, GWM,
--    GAC, Dongfeng, JAC, FAW Bestune, Livan, Kaiyi, BAIC, SWM, Soueast, Hongqi,
--    BYD) including their EVs and EREV/PHEVs (Zeekr, Li Auto, Voyah, Avatr,
--    Xpeng, Nio), plus the Russian and locally assembled lines (Lada, UAZ, GAZ,
--    Moskvich, Evolute, Aurus, Sollers, Belgee).
--
-- 2. What is actually DRIVEN: the generations sold new from ~2000 that fill the
--    used market in both countries and outnumber the new fleet many times over -
--    Toyota Camry XV30-XV70 and Corolla E120-E180, Prado 120/150, Lexus RX and
--    LX, Mercedes W203/W211/W220 and ML, VW Passat B5-B7 and Golf Mk4-Mk6,
--    Audi A4 B6-B8 and A6 C5-C7, BMW E39/E46/E60/E90/X5, Nissan, Mitsubishi,
--    Subaru, Honda, Mazda, Hyundai, Kia, Chevrolet/Daewoo/Ravon (the Kazakh and
--    Uzbek-assembled staples), Opel, Ford, Skoda, Renault, Suzuki, SsangYong,
--    Datsun, and the older Lada and GAZ lines. The bundled seed pack carries the
--    CURRENT generation of many of these and nothing older, which is the wrong
--    end of the market for a CIS driver: a 2006 Camry is a far likelier first
--    car in this app than a 2023 one.
--
-- Three things this data is NOT (CLAUDE.md hard rules 9 and 13):
--   * fuel_kinds is the model line's OFFER SET, not one car's fuel. Gazelle Next
--     is sold as petrol, diesel and CNG; that is what the array says, and Add car
--     still makes the user pick one (docs/SCHEMA.md "Vehicle catalog").
--   * every figure here is a SUGGESTION copied into the Vehicle row on Add car.
--     A user override is permanent - republishing this pack corrects what the
--     NEXT car pre-fills and never rewrites a saved garage.
--   * the server curates; it does not interpret. Nothing here is read by an
--     endpoint that decides anything about a user's data.
--
-- Ids are uuid5 over "make|model|generation" under namespace
-- 6ba7b812-9dad-11d1-80b4-00c04fd430c8, so a later correction to the same line
-- republishes the same id and updates the entry in place rather than forking it.
-- Tank/battery figures are the Russian-market specification; where a line ships
-- several battery sizes the common Russian variant is listed. ON CONFLICT keeps
-- the migration re-runnable against a table that already carries these rows.
--
-- Generations are spelled EXACTLY as the bundled seed pack spells them for the
-- lines it already carries (Lada Granta/Vesta/Largus/Niva/XRAY, UAZ Patriot).
-- Client-side overlap is resolved on make|model|generation|powertrain, not on
-- this row's id - the bundled entries have no id (docs/SYNC.md "Overlap identity
-- is the model line"). A different generation string is therefore not a
-- correction of the seed entry, it is a SECOND entry beside it, and the user
-- sees the same car twice in Add-car autocomplete.
--
-- The pack version is claimed from catalog_pack_state (migration 011), but it is
-- claimed above the BUNDLED SEED's version, not merely above the published one.
-- The client's held version starts at the seed pack's packVersion (2) and it
-- applies a pack only when packVersion is strictly greater (docs/SYNC.md
-- "packVersion is monotonic"), so a server publishing at or below the seed's
-- version is invisible: every device answers `since_version=2`, the endpoint
-- returns an honest empty delta, and this catalog would never reach a phone.
-- The seed pack and the published packs share ONE numbering space - the bundled
-- pack is a snapshot of a published one - so any migration that seeds the
-- catalog must land above the highest seed version ever shipped.

WITH next_version AS (
    SELECT GREATEST(pack_version, 2) + 1 AS v FROM catalog_pack_state WHERE singleton = 1
), seed (id, make, model, generation, years, powertrain, fuel_kinds,
         tank_capacity_l, battery_capacity_kwh) AS (VALUES
    ('0f9390ec-80e3-5b2e-9a15-cdc9ba675a5e'::uuid, 'Haval', 'Jolion', '2021-', int4range(2021, NULL, '[)'), 'ice', ARRAY['petrol95']::text[], 55, NULL::numeric),
    ('1c0dc02e-0ae7-5f88-853e-ebe5b10de655'::uuid, 'Haval', 'F7', '2019-2024', int4range(2019, 2025, '[)'), 'ice', ARRAY['petrol95']::text[], 56, NULL::numeric),
